    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0347" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg341"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stevens to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1891-02-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">Februrary 9, 1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith inclosed I transmit to the
                    Department of State a copy of resolutions adopted at a public meeting of a large
                    number of influential native-born citizens of the Hawaiian Islands, relative to
                    the death, and its attending circumstances, of the late King Kalakaua. I also
                    inclose a copy of my remarks addressed to the committee who called at this
                    legation and placed the said resolutions in my hands.</p>
                <p>I forward likewise a copy of resolutions adopted at a less numerous assemblage of
                    native Hawaiian citizens, among whom I may name John E. Bush, formerly a
                    Hawaiian minister, now editor of a native newspaper, and a present member of the
                    legislature, a half caste, B. W. Wilcox, leader of the revolutionary attempt of
                    July, 1889, and others of similar political sympathies.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John L. Stevens.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d151-a1.xml" xpointer="d151-a1"/>
